`EuclideanAlign` takes foundation-model tokens, `(window, ..., feature)`: a subject's mean and covariance are taken over all its tokens, subjects are aligned one at a time, and the output keeps the shape and float dtype of the input, so float32 window vectors now come back as float32. `channel_axis` centers each channel's tokens on the subject's mean for that channel, with one covariance per subject for `coral`.
